== What Makes Us Different ==

{| class="wikitable" style="width:100%;"
! Familiar reading pattern !! The BITwiki direction
|-
| Articles read in isolation || '''Fluid, modularized knowledge'''—coherent accounts connected through useful relationships and selectively reusable content.
|-
| One explanation for every reader || '''Simple → Core → Technical''' where different reading depths genuinely help.
|-
| Claims presented without their history || '''Evidence, provenance, and uncertainty''' remain open to examination and correction.
|-
| Knowledge as a finished product || '''Human- and AI-assisted inquiry''' can inform research and revision; publication still requires accountable sources and authority.
|}

Modularity does not mean fragmentation. A whole article must still make sense, and its individual parts must earn their place. See [[BITwiki:Book Matter|Book Matter]] and [[BITwiki:Transclusion|Transclusion]].
