== Follow a Thread ==

Every question can open another door. Begin with an existing article, follow its explanations and references, and compare related accounts without confusing an ordinary link with a proven semantic relationship.

* '''Why does something happen?''' [[Causality]] — explanations, interpretations, and disagreement.
* '''How does life maintain a boundary?''' [[Cell membrane]] — structure, transport, and regulation.
* '''How can a procedure be made precise?''' [[Algorithm]] — methods, correctness, and applications.

=== One subject, different depths ===

[[Causality/Simple|Simple orientation]] → [[Causality|Core understanding]] → [[Causality/Technical|Technical depth]]

These are different presentations of the '''same subject''', not three rival knowledge objects. Open questions belong within the appropriate account, not in an automatic fourth page. [[BITwiki:Readable depth and localization|Learn how reading depth works]].
