== 🧭 The Foundations ==

Three complementary writings, each with a different purpose:

* [[BITwiki:Manifesto|'''Manifesto''']] — why we are here.
* [[BITwiki:Four foundations|'''The Four Foundations''']] — Ontology, Epistemology, Axiology, Praxeology.
* [[BITwiki:Constitution|'''Constitution''']] — commitments that govern the undertaking.

[[BITwiki:Foundations|How these writings relate]]

The philosophical four foundations are distinct from the four conditions explored in the Manifesto. Earlier Charters remain historical sources, not competing founding authorities.
</div>

<div style="border:1px solid #e0e4e8; background:#fafbfc; border-radius:12px; padding:16px; margin-bottom:18px;">
== 🛡️ Read Critically ==

'''Evidence is signal, not truth.'''

* [[BITwiki:Evidence|Evaluate evidence]] and [[BITwiki:Sources|inspect sources]].
* [[BITwiki:Epistemic status|Check the standing of claims]] and [[BITwiki:Uncertainty|their limits]].
* [[BITwiki:Provenance|Trace origins and transformations]].

A template is not proof, and a graph edge does not become true merely because it can be displayed.
