<div style="border:1px solid #e6e6e6; background:#ffffff; border-radius:12px; padding:18px; margin-top:2px;">
== Knowledge Is Not a Dead End ==

A question leads to an explanation. An explanation points to its evidence, its limitations, and other ways of seeing the subject. Those connections make the next inquiry possible.

<pre>
question / curiosity
       ↓
inquiry · sources · competing explanations
       ↓
coherent, reviewable knowledge
       ↓
links · reuse · criticism · revision
       ↺ new questions
</pre>

'''Useful intelligence should compound.''' The [[BITwiki:Page format|page format]] keeps each account readable; [[BITwiki:Book Matter|Book Matter]] distinguishes explanation, proof, examples, methods, and references; [[BITwiki:Ontology|ontology]] and [[BITwiki:Relationships|relationships]] make carefully grounded connections possible. Material should be transcluded only when one maintained source really serves more than one context.
</div>

